.TH SSC 1
.SH NAME
ssc \- report version information and update SmartSlurmCommands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssc
.B --version
.br
.B ssc
.B --update
.RI [ --tag " " TAG ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ssc --update
resolves and installs the latest commit from the canonical GitHub main branch.
The semantic version may remain unchanged when newer unreleased commits exist.
.PP
.B ssc --update --tag
resolves and installs a specific tagged revision.
.SH REVISION TRACKING
VERSION stores the semantic release version.
BUILD_COMMIT stores the full commit SHA of the exact installed source.
Legacy installations without BUILD_COMMIT remain upgradeable and initialize it on the next update.
.PP
.B ssc --version
continues to print only the semantic version for compatibility.
.SH NETWORK
The updater queries the GitHub commit endpoint once.
When the installed commit is known and differs, it may also query the compare endpoint for a concise summary.
It downloads the archive for the resolved commit SHA, avoiding a race with a moving main branch.
.SH SAFETY
The archive is downloaded and validated in a temporary directory before installation.
The installer stages the replacement shared tree and restores the previous tree if a later installation step fails.
Update failures return nonzero and are not reported as an up-to-date state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/smartslurmcommands/VERSION
Semantic release version.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/smartslurmcommands/BUILD_COMMIT
Exact installed source revision.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Bash, curl, tar, and standard Unix tools.
Git, gh, jq, Python, and Node.js are not required.
